            title: 'Three Card Monte',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Three Card Monte is not a true game but a confidence trick: the dealer shows three cards (one is the queen), throws them face-down, and the punter bets on which is the queen. The dealer uses sleight of hand so the punter loses. Known as Find the Lady in Britain and Bonneteau in France.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Europe\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game',
